WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.501
Tensions between the US and

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.303
China are on high this morning

00:00:03.303 --> 00:00:05.138
after a blunt meeting between

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.374
the two nation's top diplomats, the first

00:00:07.574 --> 00:00:08.708
since the US shot down

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:10.543
a suspected Chinese spy balloon earlier

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:11.411
this month

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.045
and a quote,

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:13.680
very direct and candid

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.914
meeting on the sidelines

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:16.416
of the Munich Security Conference.

00:00:16.416 --> 00:00:17.684
Secretary of State

00:00:17.684 --> 00:00:18.785
Antony Blinken told

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:20.453
his counterpart Wang Yi

00:00:20.453 --> 00:00:23.089
the balloon was an unacceptable violation

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.124
of U.S. sovereignty.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.292
That must never occur again.

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.427
The State Department said.

00:00:27.427 --> 00:00:28.561
A senior official said

00:00:28.561 --> 00:00:30.330
that Blinken also criticized China

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.432
for not engaging in military

00:00:32.432 --> 00:00:34.100
to military dialog over

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.402
the incident, when Chinese

00:00:35.402 --> 00:00:36.903
military officials, quote,

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:39.239
refused to pick up the phone

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.340
and underline

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:41.908
a concern raised in earlier

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:42.909
remarks by the vice

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.411
president, Lincoln warned China

00:00:44.411 --> 00:00:46.246
there would be consequences

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.681
if they provide military aid to Russia.

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.683
In its war against Ukraine.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.285
The informal meeting came hours

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.019
after China's

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.487
top diplomat criticized

00:00:54.487 --> 00:00:56.322
the US response to the balloon.

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:57.624
In a speech to the leaders

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:58.758
attending the conference,

00:00:58.758 --> 00:01:01.861
including a bipartisan group of top U.S.

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:02.595
lawmakers.

00:01:03.863 --> 00:01:04.898
And joining me now

00:01:04.898 --> 00:01:06.866
from the Munich Security Conference,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.868
chairman of the House Foreign Affairs

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.004
Committee, Michael McCaul, and chairman

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.205
of the House Intelligence

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.807
Committee, Mike Turner.

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:16.142
Thank you both for coming on

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:18.511
Thank you, panel.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.512
So, Congressman McCaul,

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.914
I want to start with you here.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:23.149
The US-China relationship is a key

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.884
topic of discussion at the Munich summit,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:25.385
where you are

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:26.953
China's foreign minister

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.088
addressed the gathering

00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:29.556
and mocked the U.S.

00:01:29.556 --> 00:01:31.391
response to the Chinese surveillance

00:01:31.391 --> 00:01:32.525
balloon, calling it,

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.893
quote, absurd

00:01:33.893 --> 00:01:35.662
and hysterical and an effort

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:37.464
to, quote, divert attention

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.432
from its domestic problems.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:42.735
What is your response to him?

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:44.404
Well,

00:01:44.404 --> 00:01:44.671
you know,

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:47.373
I had a conversation with the secretary's

00:01:47.841 --> 00:01:48.341
team.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:50.243
I would send a very stark, stern

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.544
warning to him

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:54.180
that we will not tolerate a spy

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:55.248
born in this,

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:57.083
you know, committing espionage

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.085
over the United States again.

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.487
And I know there's

00:02:00.487 --> 00:02:02.255
talk of a private meeting,

00:02:02.255 --> 00:02:03.423
but this is a bit of a shot

00:02:03.423 --> 00:02:05.425
across the bow at this conference.

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:08.761
And I know Blinken spoke as well.

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:10.497
This is a time

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:13.233
when our relations have never been more

00:02:13.233 --> 00:02:14.734
The tension is very high right now,

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:15.902
I should say.

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:17.337
And I think the spy balloon

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:20.373
was so embarrassing, going over three

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:21.975
major military installations

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:24.244
with nuclear warheads.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.845
The idea it could capture imagery

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:26.479
and send it back

00:02:26.479 --> 00:02:28.381
to Beijing to another ship

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.316
cause a lot of damage

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:31.451
to our national security.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:32.752
But also

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:33.653
political damage

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.089
in the sense that Americans saw this

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:37.891
with the naked eye

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.894
and it was flying so low to the ground.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:42.262
And of course, the administration

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.329
has countered

00:02:43.329 --> 00:02:44.631
that it prevented the balloon

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:46.533
from being able to gather information

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:47.500
on sensitive U.S.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.702
sites and it learn valuable information

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:50.837
from studying it.

00:02:50.837 --> 00:02:52.472
And they ultimately shot it down.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:54.574
Secretary Blinken's trip to China

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.710
was delayed, canceled and China's

00:02:57.710 --> 00:02:58.945
actions were condemned.

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.413
But President Biden

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:02.148
this week stressed that the US

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:04.651
is not seeking a new Cold War with China

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.352
and said he plans to speak with President

00:03:06.352 --> 00:03:07.687
Xi at some point.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:08.855
You just heard there,

00:03:08.855 --> 00:03:09.622
Congressman Turner

00:03:09.622 --> 00:03:12.058
from Congressman McCaul, about just how

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:13.726
how the tensions are right now

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.461
between the US and China,

00:03:15.461 --> 00:03:17.363
how bad the relations are.

00:03:17.363 --> 00:03:19.599
What should his message be to.

00:03:19.599 --> 00:03:21.267
And do you think that Biden is right

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.502
to try to lower the temperature

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.737
with China in the wake of this incident?

00:03:26.973 --> 00:03:27.440
Well, remember, the

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:28.575
balloon was an escalation

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:29.542
and it was not forwarded

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.476
from its mission.

00:03:30.476 --> 00:03:31.911
It flew over our missile defense

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.546
sites, our nuclear weapons sites,

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:35.348
and then it wasn't taken out of the game

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:37.717
until the game was over. In the Atlantic.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:39.352
The reality is,

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.154
is that the administration

00:03:41.154 --> 00:03:42.021
admitted that

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:43.590
after it had shot down the balloon

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:45.058
that it should have been more proactive

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:46.359
in the three subsequent

00:03:46.359 --> 00:03:46.893
shoot downs

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:47.627
that it did

00:03:47.627 --> 00:03:48.962
of what appears to be harmless

00:03:48.962 --> 00:03:50.797
objects over North America.

00:03:50.797 --> 00:03:53.566
So the administration does have a shift

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:54.367
that it needs to take

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:55.001
in taking

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:55.668
all of this

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:56.836
a lot more serious

00:03:56.836 --> 00:03:58.738
now, being more forward

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.173
also with the American public

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:00.640
and with China

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:01.741
as to what we're facing

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.810
and what their espionage plans were.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:06.613
But, you know, here, I do think that

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:08.281
there is an opportunity

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.216
to get back to a normal dialog

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:10.850
with China.

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.118
No one, of course, wants a Cold War,

00:04:12.118 --> 00:04:13.152
but that isn't the issue.

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:14.621
What we want is a China

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:15.388
that is not going to be

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:16.656
an aggressor state

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:17.590
that's not going to be building up

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:18.191
its military

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:19.225
and threatening the United States

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:19.892
and certainly not

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.594
not making the negative comments

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:22.562
that it's making instead of

00:04:22.562 --> 00:04:24.063
just openly apologizing

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:25.398
for sending a spy balloon

00:04:25.398 --> 00:04:28.134
over our most sensitive military sites.

00:04:28.134 --> 00:04:30.370
So as we just heard, you both have been

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.704
critical of President Biden's

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:33.539
response to China here at home.

00:04:33.539 --> 00:04:34.440
But politics

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:36.943
traditionally stops at the water's edge.

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:38.878
Are you and the Biden administration

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:39.812
on the same page

00:04:39.812 --> 00:04:41.814
and presenting a united message

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:42.849
to the world

00:04:42.849 --> 00:04:44.517
when it comes to countering China,

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:45.585
where you are right now in Munich?

00:04:45.585 --> 00:04:47.320
Congressman McCaul, first to you.

00:04:48.888 --> 00:04:50.290
Yeah, I think we

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:50.590
have a

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:51.891
unique opportunity

00:04:51.891 --> 00:04:53.293
to be bipartisan

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:55.428
on this issue of,

00:04:55.428 --> 00:04:57.230
you know, national security

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.499
against one of the greatest threats to

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.900
to this country in the world

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:02.302
for that matter.

00:05:02.335 --> 00:05:03.102
And I think,

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:03.670
you know, the fact

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:05.938
that a select committee was

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.007
voted on by a large majority

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:09.075
of Democrats.

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:10.877
So when we talk about particularly export

00:05:10.877 --> 00:05:13.079
controls, this balloon,

00:05:13.079 --> 00:05:13.713
by the way,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:16.182
had a lot of American parts in it.

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:17.917
We know that the hypersonic missile

00:05:17.917 --> 00:05:18.518
that went around

00:05:18.518 --> 00:05:18.885
the world

00:05:18.885 --> 00:05:20.053
with precision

00:05:20.053 --> 00:05:21.321
was built on the backbone

00:05:21.321 --> 00:05:22.922
of American technology.

00:05:22.922 --> 00:05:25.058
So there's a lot of discussion here

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.926
at this summit about how can we

00:05:26.926 --> 00:05:27.126
you know,

00:05:27.126 --> 00:05:29.028
they steal a lot of this from us,

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.363
but we don't have to sell them

00:05:30.363 --> 00:05:31.798
the very technology

00:05:31.798 --> 00:05:33.366
they can put in their advanced weapons

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:34.233
systems

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:35.835
to then turn against either

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:37.737
Taiwan and the Pacific

00:05:37.737 --> 00:05:39.205
or eventually possibly

00:05:39.205 --> 00:05:40.973
the United States of America.

00:05:40.973 --> 00:05:42.775
I think there's great bipartisanship

00:05:42.775 --> 00:05:43.976
on this issue,

00:05:43.976 --> 00:05:45.511
by the way, as well as Ukraine.

00:05:45.511 --> 00:05:47.013
I think our delegation

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:48.448
has been very unified

00:05:48.448 --> 00:05:50.116
in our support for Ukraine

00:05:50.116 --> 00:05:52.118
and putting everything we can

00:05:52.118 --> 00:05:52.919
from a weapons

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.520
perspective in the Ukraine

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.823
so they can defeat the Russians.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.123
All right.

00:05:57.123 --> 00:05:58.224
Let's turn to Ukraine.

00:05:58.224 --> 00:05:59.859
As you mentioned, Congressman McCaul,

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.394
it is a big talker there at the summit.

00:06:01.394 --> 00:06:03.162
I remember last year

00:06:03.162 --> 00:06:04.530
everyone was talking about Russia

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:05.531
getting ready to invade.

00:06:05.531 --> 00:06:07.834
Now, it's been nearly a year.

00:06:08.401 --> 00:06:10.970
And nearly a dozen members in your party

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:11.704
have introduced

00:06:11.704 --> 00:06:12.638
a so-called

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:15.475
Ukraine fatigue resolution to end U.S.

00:06:15.475 --> 00:06:16.909
support for Ukraine.

00:06:16.909 --> 00:06:18.411
And a new poll is showing support

00:06:18.411 --> 00:06:19.645
among Americans for arming

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:21.314
Ukraine is dropping.

00:06:21.314 --> 00:06:22.315
How concerned,

00:06:22.315 --> 00:06:24.450
Congressman McCall are foreign leaders?

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.017
You're speaking

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:26.519
to that American support

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.154
for Ukraine, particularly

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:30.456
within your own party, is weakening

00:06:33.126 --> 00:06:34.660
Well, I know that Bill

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.730
had about ten co-sponsors out of 435

00:06:38.131 --> 00:06:39.031
members of Congress.

00:06:39.031 --> 00:06:39.632
I would say that

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:41.434
support is still very strong.

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.803
And this delegation is bipartisan,

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:46.005
very strong support for Ukraine.

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.373
I think we're you're seeing a split

00:06:47.373 --> 00:06:48.908
from the administration, though.

00:06:48.908 --> 00:06:50.309
And I have to say, well,

00:06:50.309 --> 00:06:52.211
this is bipartisan as well.

00:06:52.211 --> 00:06:53.446
Is that for the past year,

00:06:53.446 --> 00:06:55.114
we've been very slow

00:06:55.114 --> 00:06:56.182
in getting these weapons

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:58.418
in in the name of being too provocative,

00:06:58.785 --> 00:07:00.787
whether it be stingers, jab ones, these

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:02.555
short range artillery,

00:07:02.555 --> 00:07:04.557
no longer range artillery attack.

00:07:04.557 --> 00:07:06.626
And they can take out the Iranian drones

00:07:06.626 --> 00:07:10.129
in Crimea and also aviation like F-16.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.764
If we put this stuff in

00:07:11.764 --> 00:07:13.866
from the very beginning of this conflict,

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:15.301
a year from now

00:07:15.301 --> 00:07:16.469
may have been very different

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:17.003
as we look

00:07:17.003 --> 00:07:19.539
at the anniversary on February 24th.

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.507
The longer they drag this out

00:07:21.507 --> 00:07:23.109
they play into Putin's hands.

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:23.843
He wants this

00:07:23.843 --> 00:07:25.745
to be a long, protracted war

00:07:25.745 --> 00:07:28.314
because he knows that potentially

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.081
he'll lose.

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:30.116
We could lose the will

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.384
of the American people.

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.552
And therefore the Congress.

00:07:32.552 --> 00:07:34.086
And we're seeing the same dynamic

00:07:34.086 --> 00:07:35.755
in the European Parliament's

00:07:35.755 --> 00:07:37.290
strong support now.

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.926
But they're worried that if this doesn't

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:42.061
end with the resolution you know, sooner

00:07:42.061 --> 00:07:43.396
rather than later,

00:07:43.396 --> 00:07:45.465
this will be an issue for us.

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:48.100
Yeah, and you mentioned the need

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.170
for Ukraine to have more weapons to fight

00:07:51.204 --> 00:07:51.637
Russia, a

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:53.005
bipartisan group in Congress,

00:07:53.005 --> 00:07:54.040
including some members

00:07:54.040 --> 00:07:55.441
on your own committee,

00:07:55.441 --> 00:07:56.642
wrote to President Biden

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.978
urging him to give Ukraine F-16

00:07:58.978 --> 00:08:00.246
fighter jets.

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:01.180
You said the US

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:02.348
should give Ukraine, quote,

00:08:02.348 --> 00:08:04.951
everything they need to win this thing.

00:08:05.485 --> 00:08:06.152
Congressman McCaul,

00:08:06.152 --> 00:08:07.320
do you believe the administration

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.055
is considering taking that step

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:12.725
You know, I hope so.

00:08:12.725 --> 00:08:13.626
The attack himself

00:08:13.626 --> 00:08:15.962
had been on the table for months

00:08:15.962 --> 00:08:17.463
and they have sent those in.

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.532
And the same delivery applies to attack.

00:08:19.565 --> 00:08:21.601
And those are the high MOIS.

00:08:21.601 --> 00:08:23.102
But, you know, the fact is,

00:08:23.102 --> 00:08:24.504
the longer they wait,

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:25.338
the longer this

00:08:25.338 --> 00:08:27.406
this conflict will prevail.

00:08:28.341 --> 00:08:30.776
I honestly, every top military expert

00:08:30.776 --> 00:08:32.879
I talked to at this conference

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:35.014
agreed with what I was saying.

00:08:35.014 --> 00:08:37.350
And I think, you know, Mike Turner,

00:08:37.350 --> 00:08:38.251
that we need to throw

00:08:38.251 --> 00:08:40.920
everything we can into this fight

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.021
so that they can win.

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.422
And once he's going to tell us

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:44.357
that soon as well,

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.759
he had a speech here at the conference

00:08:46.759 --> 00:08:48.561
saying the same thing.

00:08:48.561 --> 00:08:50.463
And I think the momentum is building

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:52.131
for this to happen.

